# reference.in: this family's reference requirements, resolved to the exact, hashed reference.lock
# beside this file by `python -m rcp_ndcg_test.jobs.reference_lock` (owner decision 35). The tool
# constrains torch and the CUDA stack to the engine image's freeze; every other pin installs into
# the family's reference venv and takes precedence over the image's copy. Never edit the lock by hand.
# The reference environment for the pplx-embed-v1 family's reference.py, in ITS OWN
# python (never the harness's process, never the engine image):
#   pip install -r reference.lock
# The wave runner points --reference-python at this environment (the node's bootstrap
# installs it over the image's torch -- decision 2: run on the image's torch, install
# only what is missing); the reference subprocess runs while the engine on that slot is
# up and releases its memory when it exits. `--mode render` needs only huggingface_hub
# and tokenizers (it reads the pinned config.json, tokenizer_config.json and
# tokenizer.json, and runs the card's cut in the tokenizers library) and runs in any
# interpreter that has them.
#
# The checkpoint ships no requirements.txt of its own; these are the card's two imports
# (`SentenceTransformer(repo, trust_remote_code=True)`; the card's usage and its
# "Using SentenceTransformers" section) with the checkpoint's own floor:
# config.json `transformers_version` is "5.0.0.dev0", and the remote modeling.py uses
# transformers 5.x APIs (`processing_utils.Unpack`, `masking_utils.create_causal_mask`).
